      "test.claim.compiler_frontend_program_status_witness",
      "test.claim.self_host_compile_phase_frontier_witness",
      "test.claim.self_host_compile_phase_live_gate_witness"
    ],
    measurement: "gunbc#10094 measured this enrolment as a large WIN and withdrew it anyway; the refusal is DESIGN section 3, not cost -- gunbc#10108 removes the receipt-series argument instead of paying to reify and verify it per consuming frame, so one fact gets one row at the declaration that makes it cheap",
    next_trigger: "none that restores THIS spelling: the general declaration takes the series as an argument and is meant to keep taking it. The row retires when its repair lands, and re-proposing this producer means proposing to serve the argument-taking shape again"
  },
  RefusedShareCandidate {
    producer: "v2.std.node_reflection.coproduct_arm_keys",
    verdict: KeyOmitsAnInputTheValueDependsOn {
      undeclared_input: "the RESOLVING CONTEXT. coproduct_arm_keys(type_name: Symbol) reaches resolve_type_node, whose host arm eval_resolve_type_node calls type_item_by_name(ctx, type_name); that fold iterates ctx.modules and matches on the AUTHORED (bare) name. So the value is a function of type_name AND of which modules the claim scope carries and which bare name wins among them. The cross-claim memo key is (fn_node, args_hash) and args_hash covers the declared arguments only, so ctx is invisible to it" as String,
    },
    carrier_modules: [
      "v2.test.claim.affected_set_universe",
      "v2.test.claim.generated_conformance_floor",
      "v2.test.manual.value_null_split_witness",
      "v2.test.manual.coproduct_reflection_conformance"
    ],
    measurement: concat("The refusal is a SOUNDNESS verdict and does not rest on the cost figures, which are reported because the census is what named the producer: required floor run 34742966153, artifact required-floor-cross-claim-demand (required_floor_cross_claim_demand.tsv), the row keyed producer=coproduct_arm_keys arg_shape=keyed, decl_site src/v2/std/node_reflection.dag. ITS COST COLUMNS ARE NOT COPIED HERE (DESIGN section 6: name the instrument, never transcribe its output). The run, the artifact and the row key above ARE the citation; a figure copied into this prose is unreachable from the producer that owns it and rots without anyone touching either end. THE DECIDING OBSERVATION IS IN THE SAME ARTIFACT AND IS NOT A COST FIGURE: that file carries SEVERAL keyed rows for this producer, one per distinct type_name, and one of them reports a consumer-module count ABOVE ONE, over v2.test.claim.generated_conformance_floor and v2.test.manual.value_null_split_witness. Claims of different modules carry different scopes (claim_scope_for prepares per module), so that row is the shape a cross-SCOPE serve would take if this producer were enrolled. IT IS NOT A SERVE TODAY AND THIS ROW DOES NOT CLAIM ONE: cross_claim_pure_admitted gates storing on the roster, so an unenrolled producer is re-derived and never served, and the census column reports cross-claim DEMAND rather than sharing. An earlier revision of this sentence said the cross-scope serve was ALREADY OCCURRING; that was wrong in the direction that flatters the refusal, and is corrected here rather than deleted. The refusal is therefore PREVENTIVE and the harm is unobserved: enrolling is what would make the key load-bearing, and the failure mode it would admit is not a refusal. WHAT THE SEAM ACTUALLY DOES WAS EXECUTED RATHER THAN READ OFF THE RUST, and the two specimens do not behave alike (witty-otter-157, 2026-09-13): for one it ANSWERS from one of several candidate declarations -- a coproduct in one module and a record in another, with an enrolled claim green on main over the arm list it returned -- and for the other it FAILS UNTYPED with an unknown-closed-type host error rather than picking between two disjoint arm sets. So the mechanism is: answers from one of several, or fails untyped, NEVER refuses. An earlier revision of this row said first-match-wins serves a plausible wrong arm set; that is true of the first shape only, and was read from the Rust rather than run. Neither shape is a typed located refusal, which is why the defect and this refusal both stand unchanged ", homonym_census_note()),
    next_trigger: "REFLECTION KEYED BY QUALIFIED OR SCOPED IDENTITY, as a capability and not as a witness. Either type_item_by_name resolves a QUALIFIED name so the value is a function of its arguments alone, or the reflection carries the resolving scope into the key so the memo can tell two resolutions apart. A scope-invariance witness is explicitly NOT the trigger: it is validation standing where construction is available (DESIGN section 5), the value would still be computed from an input the key cannot see, and a witness over today's corpus says nothing about tomorrow's homonym. Bare-name resolution is a namespace-layer subject (gunbc.rung_drop bare_name_fork_lens and the namespace cut), so this trigger is an upstream obligation rather than work this roster can do. When it lands, this producer and the two rows below return as enrolments with the ordinary present-versus-absent receipt" as String
  },
